t doofenshmirtz goes to while trying  to protect vanessa  disney fairy tales tend to stay away  from lewdness keeping in mind their very  young audience most disney villains are  motivated by pg-13 impulses like a  desire for magical power or wealth not  so with judge frollo the main villain of  1996 is the hunchback of notre dame  frollo was all kinds of messed up as the  minister of justice frollo was highly  disturbed by the unusual passions  awakening in his bosom at the sight of  the beautiful esmerelda in fact frollo  sings an entire song hellfire about how  hot he is for esmerelda how his feelings  are her fault and how he will not rest  until he gets with her whether she's  into him or not  it's extremely disturbing watching a  disney character sing about his desire  to assault the heroine how this film got  a g rating is a mystery to everyone  sid phillips from 1995's toy story  managed to be a terrifying villain  despite only being an 11 year old kid  that was because sid delighted in  breaking apart toys and reconstructing  them in grotesque horrific ways the  obvious pleasure sid takes in mutilating  beautiful little toys would sound alarm  bells for any psychiatrist as well as  child protective services sid displays  classic signs of a child who has  suffered neglect and abuse  in the movie we get a brief glimpse of  sid's father asleep on a reclining chair  a deer head mounted on the wall shows  that mr phillips likes to inflict  violence on others the fact that he is  asleep in the middle of the day shows he  is likely jobless and the many empty  beer cans littering the room likely  indicate an alcoholic who doesn't take  care of his surroundings all these hints  alongside sid's fear of waking his  father up point towards the philips  household being an unhappy one how much  of sid's sadistic impulses are the  result of his father may be debatable  but this much is clear the kid is  seeking an outlet for his anger by  herding toys  disney often makes use of pop culture  icons while creating their animated  characters a trend that included 2016's  moana via tamatoa a giant flamboyant  crab that craves shiny valuable objects  for older viewers tamatoa's look might  evoke memories of iconic glam rock  singer songwriter david bowie and that  is no accident the look of tamatoa was  in fact based on bowie and the  character's big musical number shiny was  written with bowie in mind as the film  songwriter lin manuel miranda told  people in 2016 i'd been listening to  bowie on a loop i was like well i'm  writing a glam rock tune for this crap  this jewel encrusted crab to channel the  spirit of bowie further tamatoa was  voiced by new zealand's jermaine clement  who has been known to bust out a  credible impression of bowie in projects  like flight of the concords clement told  the au review when i tried to record  shiny in the character's voice miranda  just kept pushing the bowie thing do it  more bowie he wanted glam like a t-rex  bowie  ursula from 1989's the little mermaid is  as rollickingly entertaining as a disney  villain can get which makes sense  because she was based on a rollickingly  entertaining drag queen rob minkoff  animator for the little mermaid revealed  in the 2020 disney plus documentary  howard that he came up with a host of  possible designs for ursula's character  including one based on famed drag queen  divine best known for playing edna in  1988's hairspray when the film's  lyricist howard ashman saw the drawings  the choice was clear and that design was  put on a board with a bunch of other  designs and then the day that howard  ashman came in to look at the designs he  zeroed in on that one truly divine  1994's the lion king is generally agreed  to be one of the greatest disney movies  of all time despite being a story about  talking animals the movie was grounded  in mature themes as it took its cues  from the biblical stories of joseph and  moses william shakespeare's hamlet and  also from the infamous nazi propaganda  films of lenny riefenstahl in the song  be prepared sung by the movie's main bad  guy scar we see hyenas marching past the  villainous lion in a highly regimented  style the movements of the hyenas and  the view of their formations was based  specifically on nazi propaganda films by  riefenstahl according to entertainment  weekly the idea for the song came from a  sketch by story staffer jorgen clabin  that pictured scar as hitler which  inspired the directors to craft the be  prepared sequence which became one of  the most iconic parts of the film pixar  is a studio that excels in telling  stories filled with warmth and empathy  stanley kubrick was a filmmaker renowned  for telling stories filled with tension  coldness and dread the two might not  seem to have much of an overlap at first  blush but 2008's wally brought the two  together in an unexpected manner through  the introduction of its main villain in  wali the central antagonist is a rogue  ai called auto that has control of a  vessel carrying humanity into the  furthest reaches of space otto's looks  and personality are clearly based on the  villainous hal 9000 from kubrick's 2001  a space odyssey but the references don't  end there a scene from 2001 where an ape  learns to use tools features the same  music as the scene in wall-e when the  captain of otto's space vessel finally  leaves his chair to stand on his feet  learning self-reliance in the process  after having depended on otto for  everything for so many years  2005's disney film chicken little was a  heartfelt story about growing up  standing up for your beliefs and  learning to let your children become  self-reliant and it also paid homage to  one of the most influential terrifying  sci-fi novels of all time h.g wells 1897  masterpiece the war of the worlds which  features aliens landing in terrifying  tripods fortunately the machines in  chicken little were a lot more benign  than the ones that showed up in the war  of the worlds it is revealed in the  final act of the movie that the aliens  initially visited earth just to gather  acorns and later returned with an entire  armada because they thought one of their  own was being held hostage by earthlings  once the misunderstanding is cleared up  the aliens returned peacefully to their  home planet  for multiple generations of children the  tom and jerry cartoons have been a  popular retelling of the classic david  vs goliath narrative in this case the  big dimwitted cat tom is the evil  goliath while the smaller quick-witted  jerry is plucky little david who humbles  the giant with his brains and willpower  but is the story really that simple once  you grow up and need to look into buying  or renting your own house you begin to  realize what a major problem house pests  like mice can be which is why house pets  like cats are used to eliminate pests  and keep the home safe once you start  looking at the situation from that angle  you realize that jerry was the villain  of the show an uninvited house pest that  ran roughshod all over the house eating  and taking whatever he wanted meanwhile  tom was simply the house pet trying to  do what it had been trained to  accomplish keeping the home safe from  unwanted rodents sure tom was always  left frustrated after his encounters  with jerry but just imagine how tom's  owners must have felt so if you think  jerry is the good guy all we can say is  adult innuendo in cartoons aimed at  children is not a new thing but  sometimes the innuendo is so in your  face you can't help but be surprised by  the audacity of the show's writers case  in point roxy rocket's appearance in the  new batman adventures where she had a  singular obsession with getting laid in  the episode the ultimate thrill viewers  are introduced to roxy a daredevil stunt  woman who turned to a life of crime to  satisfy her craving for excitement in  roxy's mind her reaction to danger is  quite similar to arousal roxy's weapon  of choice is a giant phallic rocket and  she soon becomes obsessed with batman  throughout the episode roxy makes one  charged comment after another telling  penguin about batman quote i was the  best he ever had and i love a man with  staying power but the most brazen scene  comes at the end when roxy's last daring  heist is stopped by batman she appears  to be in the throes of ecstasy me and  you  yeah  yeah  yeah 2010's despicable me had you  rooting for the bad guy felonious gru  was an aspiring supervillain who dreamed  of pulling off the ultimate heist to  prove himself so he was forced to go to  the bank of evil an organization that  offers loans to supervillains who can  prove their schemes are sufficiently  evil however the entrance to the bank is  hidden behind a urinal but the truly  dastardly touch is that the entrance is  behind the middle urinal when you go to  a public restroom most people's instinct  is to use the urinal to the left or the  right because that minimizes the chance  of having to pee standing next to  someone only someone truly evil and  twisted would willingly use the middle  urinal where he could be flanked on both  sides by others it is exactly that kind  of dastardly mind that the bank of evil  would be interested in doing business  with  the evil queen from 1937 snow white and  the seven dwarves might just be the most  iconic disney villain of all time  she's often portrayed as the  personification of evil but adults might  be more likely to diagnose her as  suffering from narcissistic personality  disorder npd also referred to as  megalomania is a mental condition which  has been officially recognized by the  american psychiatric association people  suffering from npd have an exaggerated  sense of their own importance as well as  a deep need for excessive attention and  admiration this in turn leads to the  sufferer having trouble maintaining  relationships due to a lack of empathy  for others these symptoms fit the evil  queen to a t the tragic part is npd is  actually treatable but the people who  suffer from it have such a high opinion  of themselves that they refuse to  recognize they have a problem that  requires therapy the evil queen's time  could have been put to much better use  if she had stopped obsessing over snow  white so much and booked an appointment  with the dwarf named doc instead  check out one of our newest videos right  here plus even more looper videos about  your favorite villains are coming soon  subscribe to our youtube channel and hit  the bell so you don't miss a single one

